---
description: Runtime rules for the Chrome extension, Frank, evidence, targeting, and Report Bug
alwaysApply: false
globs:
  - "apps/extension/**"
  - "packages/frank/**"
  - "packages/rules/**"
  - "packages/ai/**"
  - "packages/findings/**"
  - "tests/**"
---
When changing extension runtime behavior:

- Keep scans deterministic and useful without AI.
- Keep Chrome built-in AI separate from the scan lifecycle; Rescan must never be an AI recovery action.
- Keep Frank task sessions isolated by finding/site.
- Keep local-AI output bounded by verified evidence and deterministic remediation families.
- Prefer no spotlight over a confidently wrong spotlight.
- Treat open Shadow DOM, rerenders, stale targets, hidden targets and ambiguity as explicit runtime states.
- Report Bug must stay privacy bounded by default: no cookies, form values, credentials, full DOM, unrestricted page content, selectors or URL query contents.
- Measurement sources and reference/enrichment sources are not interchangeable.
